  "title": "What Does a Medicaid Notice Actually Look Like?",
  "summary": "Medicaid notices come in many forms - coverage denials, fair-hearing rights, copay changes, plan assignments, service authorizations, and the annual renewal - but they share a problem: each one asks someone, often someone managing a chronic condition, working two jobs, or caring for a child, to understand what's happening and frequently to act on it.",
